# Which process can write each GPS log string -- decided OFFLINE by grepping the images this port
# ships (2026-09-23). Written for scripts/device/zl1-gps-probe.sh section 3, whose comment points
# here. Host-side and read-only; no device was involved (it is in EDL).

## rule

  A log string can only appear in the log of the process whose address space contains it.
  A vendor library loaded by a process in the Android container -> logcat.
  A UT-side binary, or the library it dlopens -> stderr -> the systemd journal of its unit.
  A string in NO binary -> a count of 0 for it is not evidence about anything, ever.

## the images searched

  /mnt/utrootfs          /dev/loop0 /mnt/utrootfs
  /mnt/android-sys-test  /dev/loop7 /mnt/android-sys-test
  /mnt/vendor-ro         /dev/loop9 /mnt/vendor-ro

