## side C -- the two patterns that were REMOVED, and why a 0 for them was never evidence

### set_gps_service_callbacks
  UT rootfs     : 0
  Android system: 0
  Android vendor: 0
  searched as a fixed string, recursively, case-sensitively, over every regular file in the image
  (grep reads the whole file, so a name surviving only as an exported symbol would still show up
   here -- this one is in no binary in any image, symbol tables included)
  -> zero in all three, and zero is what it always was. Counting it told the probe nothing
     about any process on this path; it is not a log line at all (it is a name from the
     vendor HAL's API, and not one that survived into the images either).

### Unable to get GPS service
  UT rootfs     : 0
  Android system: 2
  Android vendor: 0
  searched as a fixed string, recursively, case-sensitively, over every regular file in the image

  This one IS present -- but not on this path. Where it lives:
    /mnt/android-sys-test/lib/libandroid_servers.so
    /mnt/android-sys-test/lib64/libandroid_servers.so
    and in the UT rootfs (the daemon and the library it loads): 0
    -> libandroid_servers.so is the FRAMEWORK's GnssLocationProvider. The UT daemon does not
       go through it: providers/gps/android_hardware_abstraction_layer.cpp calls
       IGnss::getService() over HIDL itself. So a 0 from that string says nothing about this
       path -- and the earlier probe read exactly that 0 as 'the provider was never
       instantiated'.

## what the probe prints now, from the same three groups

  logcat  block: locClientOpen failed / Failed to get features supported / gnssSetCapabilitesCb
                 (gnssSetCapabilitesCb is also in libandroid_servers.so, but on this path the
                  writer is the vendor impl android.hardware.gnss@1.0-impl-qti.so in the
                  container -- logcat either way)
                 (+ 'Failed to checking QMI_LOC message supported', still logcat-owned)
  journal block: Issue instantiating provider / Instantiating and configuring /
                 Remote service failed to start / Failed to inject reference time /
                 android_hardware_abstraction_layer
  gates:         the trust-store messages above, journal-owned, next to the daemon's environ

## how to reproduce

  sh scripts/host/zl1-gps-selftest.sh          # 59 checks, no device
  and, for the counts above, the same greps this file was produced by:
  grep -rlaF -- 'locClientOpen failed' /mnt/android-sys-test /mnt/vendor-ro
  grep -rlaF -- 'Issue instantiating provider' /mnt/utrootfs
